WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.835
-I'm Steve Higgins,
and we're about to play

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.870
a game called Phone Booth, and
our first player of the evening

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.138
is the host
of "The Tonight Show",

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:07.273
Mr. Jimmy Fallon!

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.977
[ Cheering ]

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.847
And Jimmy's opponent is a judge
on "America's Got Talent"

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.315
and the star of the new show,
"L.A.'s Finest",

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:17.817
it's Gabrielle Union!

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:21.988
[ Cheering ]

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.723
The rules of this game
are very simple.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.825
I'll be asking of you
trivia questions,

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:29.095
and if you get a wrong answer, a
stranger from our mystery bench

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.931
gets shoved into your phone
booth.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.333
Simple as that.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.601
First question is for Jimmy.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.870
[ Buttons clicking ]

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.307
[ Telephone ringing ]

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.042
-Hello?

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.176
-Jimmy.
-Yes.

00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:46.446
-If you combine
the Jonas Brothers

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.447
and the Hemsworth brothers,

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:51.151
how many brothers do you have?

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.119
Jonas Brothers, Hemsworth --

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.587
-Plus Hemsworths?
-Yes.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.321
-I know there's three Jonas

00:00:56.321 --> 00:00:58.424
plus the bonus Jonas.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:03.096
Four Jonas brothers, and, um,
Liam, Chris...

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.531
Seven.
-Seven. Wait.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:06.532
[ Bell dings ]

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:07.967
There you go! You go it right!

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:11.270
[ Cheering ]

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.339
-I know my Jonas Brothers!
-All right!

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.308
Well, joining Gabrielle's booth

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.443
is a DJ, songwriter,
record producer

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:20.646
who's new album,
"Father of Asahd" is out now.

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:22.315
Give it up for DJ Khaled!

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.985
[ Cheering ]

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.352
-Oh!

00:01:27.352 --> 00:01:30.690
[ Cheering continues ]

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.725
-Come in my booth! Hey, baby!

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:36.829
-How you doing?
-Come on in!

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:37.763
-Wait, I want --

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:39.499
I want him in my booth.
-No.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.834
-I would say it would've been
a problem about a year ago,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.903
but I'm on Weight Watchers now,
so we good.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.871
You know what I'm saying?
-You are tiny!

00:01:45.871 --> 00:01:47.306
-Thank you.
-You're wasting away.

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:48.675
-They call me "Slim Jim"!

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.609
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:53.379
-Next question is for Gabrielle.
-Okay.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.780
-[ Whispering ] How you doing?
-I'm good.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.816
[ Telephone rings ]

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.917
Hello?

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.485
-Gabrielle...
-Yes.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:00.987
-Green Mamba...
-Uh-huh.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.656
-...European asp,
and fer-de-lance

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.425
are all species of what animal?

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:07.726
-Snake.

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:09.128
-Judges.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:11.430
[ Bell dings ]
Yes! The correct answer!

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.899
It was snake!

00:02:13.899 --> 00:02:17.170
Joining Jimmy's booth,
animal expert Grant Kemmerer

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.872
and his 10-foot Burmese python
Sheila!

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:21.874
[ Cheering ]

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:25.244
Don't worry. Come on up.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:26.846
Get right in there.
-Jimmy!

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.616
-Hey, buddy.
Nice to see you, pal.

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.084
-Hey, buddy.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.155
-You okay?

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.857
-Hey, man.
-How you doing?

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:41.160
-Great. It's all good.
-Okay, next question.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.329
-Oh, my gosh, are you joking me?

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.298
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:46.633
Is that your hand?

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:51.570
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.007
-All right, the next question
is for Jimmy.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.274
-Yes.

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:56.609
[ Telephone ringing ]

00:02:56.609 --> 00:03:00.479
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:01.713
-You want me to get it?

00:03:01.713 --> 00:03:03.515
[ Cheering, laughter ]

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:10.088
[ Ringing continues ]

00:03:10.088 --> 00:03:12.825
-[ Laughing ] Sorry, there was
a snake on the phone.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.260
-Or are you just happy
to see me?

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.928
Jimmy!

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:20.233
Where in the body
is the coccyx bone.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:21.501
The coccyx bone.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.768
The coccyx!

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:23.903
-The butt.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.638
-Coccyx bone.
-You think so?

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.108
-What part of the body...
-Uh...that'd be, uh --

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.509
that'd be in butt.

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:31.811
-[ Laughing ] In the butt?

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.079
In the butt! Judges?

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.048
[ Bell dings ]
Yes! It is the butt bone!

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.715
[ Cheering ]

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:40.419
Well, joining Gabrielle's booth
is the Grammy-winning musician

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:43.356
with a new album called
"Wah Gwaan?!"

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.224
This summer,
he's on tour with UB40,

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.493
make some room for Shaggy!

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.762
[ Cheering ]

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.164
-Yo!

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.399
-Hey!

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.035
-Shaggy!
-Oh, my gosh!

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:59.005
-Why am I getting --
What is going on?!

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.572
-All right! Hi, [indistinct].

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:03.809
-Wait, what is happening?!
-Lovely.

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:04.944
You get Khaled and Shaggy,

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.246
I have a 12-foot python
in my thing.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:08.681
This is...rigged.

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.216
-Those are the rules
of the game.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.617
-Look like you having fun.
-What?!

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:14.520
-Shaggy didn't get it wrong.
It wasn't him. Okay!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.555
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:19.424
Next question is for Gabrielle.

00:04:19.424 --> 00:04:21.460
[ Telephone ringing ]

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.929
-Hello.
-Yes.

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:25.365
Gabrielle,
what would take longer --

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.767
watching every episode
of "Game of Thrones"

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:31.804
or every Marvel superhero movie?

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.806
-Uh, uh, uh, uh...

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.707
So, "Game of Thrones" --
every episode --

00:04:35.707 --> 00:04:38.044
that's eight seasons.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.678
How many Marvel movies?
-I have no idea.

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:41.214
-I've only watched
"Black Panther".

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:42.681
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:44.316
Uh...uh, uh...
-There's a lot.

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:45.751
-"Game of Thrones", right?
"Game of Thrones".

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:46.885
[ Slide whistle ]
-Answer?

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:48.087
-"Game of Thrones".
-"Game of Thrones".

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.722
-"Game of Thrones" is correct!
[ Bell dings ]

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:52.891
[ Cheering ]

00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:55.827
Joining Jimmy's booth, he plays
Grey Worm on "Game of Thrones"

00:04:55.827 --> 00:04:57.230
and a recording artist

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.031
under the name
of Raleigh Ritchie

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.467
it's Jacob Anderson!
-Oh, my God!

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.768
[ Cheering ]

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:04.269
Yo!
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:04.269 --> 00:05:07.906
[ Cheering continues ]

00:05:07.906 --> 00:05:10.042
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]
Big fan.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:11.911
Thank you for being
inside of my booth.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.180
-This is --
-We got each other,

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.414
we got each other.

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.349
We have each other,
we have each other.

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:19.018
-Hold me. Yeah. All right.
[ Dial tone ]

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.220
-We all know what that means.
It's time for the final call.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.288
-Okay.
-And the winner

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:24.122
of this next question...
-[ Chuckles ]

00:05:24.122 --> 00:05:26.826
...gets to shove everyone else
from the mystery bench

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:28.661
into their opponent's booth.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.096
So let's bring out the bench.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.897
First, they're Olympic figure
skaters

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:33.766
and hosts of
"Wedding Cake Championship",

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:37.636
which premiers June 3rd at 10:00
p.m. on the Food Network.

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:40.106
Please welcome Johnny Weir
and Tara Lipinski!

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:45.811
[ Cheering ]

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:47.647
Plus...
-Hi, guys.

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:49.481
-Hi, buddy, how are you?
-...we've got two contortionists

00:05:49.481 --> 00:05:52.652
from the Big Apple Circus,
Ellie and Ekaterina!

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:57.723
[ Cheering ]

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.758
-And from the
City of Brotherly Love,

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:03.062
it's the Phillie Phanatic!

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:06.232
-[ Chiming ]

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.733
-All right, final question...

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.469
-Who moved the door?!
Was that the snake?

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:12.070
-Who moved the door?
-...is for Jimmy.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.940
[ Telephone ringing ]

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.874
-I can't even pick up the phone.

00:06:15.874 --> 00:06:17.910
[ Ringing continues ]
-I'll let it ring.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.544
We can wait.

00:06:19.544 --> 00:06:22.415
[ Ringing continues ]

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:24.250
-Hello?
-Jimmy.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.552
-Yes.
-Name three English words

00:06:27.552 --> 00:06:31.991
that rhyme with pickle.
-Come on.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:34.092
-I can't think of one.
-Sprinkle.

00:06:34.092 --> 00:06:35.294
Sickle.
-Trickle.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:36.962
-Sickle.
-Sickle, yes.

00:06:36.962 --> 00:06:38.364
-Tickle.
-Tickle.

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:39.698
-Two.
-Nickle.

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:41.200
-Nickle!
-Nickle, yes!

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.802
[ Bell dings ]
-Yay!

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.371
[ Cheering ]

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:47.273
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]
-That means Jimmy wins!

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:50.910
Let's see how many people we can
get into Gabrielle's booth. Oh!

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:57.416
-Open wide. [ Laughs ]

00:06:57.416 --> 00:06:59.252
-Please, however you can fit
in there.

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.619
-Oh, God.

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:02.554
-Oh, of course.

00:07:02.554 --> 00:07:05.390
[ Laughs ] Oh, my God.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.926
-Oh, my God.
-I don't -- Oh, it's a foot.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:09.729
-Are you okay? Can I help you?

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:13.032
Can you get in in any way?
Oh, my God, all right,

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:16.269
Johnny next to the
contortionist.

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:17.503
Go the Phanatic!

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:19.037
Phillie Phanatic,
can you get any --

00:07:19.037 --> 00:07:20.906
-Phillie Phanatic,
just get your arm in there.

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:22.207
-That's it, right there.
There you go!

00:07:22.207 --> 00:07:23.442
There's our winner!

00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:27.079
My thanks to Gabrielle Union,
DJ Khaled,

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:30.249
Grant Kemmerer,
Jacob Anderson, Shaggy,

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:33.319
Johnny Weir, Tara Lipinski,
the Big Apple Circus,

00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:35.054
and the Philadelphia Phillies.

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:36.889
More "Tonight Show"
after the break!

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:41.326
[ Cheering ]

00:07:41.326 --> 00:07:48.401
[ Cheering continues ]

